1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,160
Why does resting in your own home

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:03,740
feel like getting caught?

3
00:00:03,750 --> 00:00:06,800
Picture this. You hear keys at the

4
00:00:06,810 --> 00:00:09,300
front door. A second ago, you were

5
00:00:09,310 --> 00:00:10,360
watching a movie.

6
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:12,440
Now you're washing a plate.

7
00:00:12,450 --> 00:00:14,730
The plate was already clean.

8
00:00:15,862 --> 00:00:18,542
An hour earlier, this evening looked different.

9
00:00:19,042 --> 00:00:20,042
Dinner was done.

10
00:00:20,742 --> 00:00:22,342
The urgent stuff was handled.

11
00:00:23,042 --> 00:00:25,902
You texted a friend: finally, movie time.

12
00:00:26,522 --> 00:00:28,602
You made a snack, found the remote,

13
00:00:28,802 --> 00:00:30,402
and gave yourself twenty minutes.

14
00:00:31,142 --> 00:00:33,052
Then you noticed your laptop was still

15
00:00:33,062 --> 00:00:33,582
open.

16
00:00:34,245 --> 00:00:35,845
One unanswered email.

17
00:00:36,565 --> 00:00:38,165
It could wait until tomorrow.

18
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:39,325
You knew that.

19
00:00:39,885 --> 00:00:41,845
But answering it would take two minutes.

20
00:00:42,645 --> 00:00:44,435
Then you could relax without it hanging

21
00:00:44,445 --> 00:00:47,065
over you. You put the snack down,

22
00:00:47,265 --> 00:00:49,075
crossed the room, and pulled the chair

23
00:00:49,085 --> 00:00:49,545
out.

24
00:00:50,131 --> 00:00:51,191
You sent the reply.

25
00:00:52,011 --> 00:00:53,091
Another message arrived.

26
00:00:54,031 --> 00:00:56,691
Apparently your inbox had learned to reproduce.

27
00:00:57,671 --> 00:00:59,031
You opened that one too.

28
00:00:59,611 --> 00:01:01,131
Now you needed a document.

29
00:01:01,691 --> 00:01:03,371
The document needed a correction.

30
00:01:04,111 --> 00:01:05,981
Your movie was still waiting for you

31
00:01:05,991 --> 00:01:06,831
to press play.

32
00:01:07,431 --> 00:01:08,951
The snack was getting cold.

33
00:01:09,837 --> 00:01:11,017
Your phone rang.

34
00:01:11,837 --> 00:01:12,317
The timer.

35
00:01:12,897 --> 00:01:14,037
Twenty minutes were up.

36
00:01:14,557 --> 00:01:16,827
You had successfully completed your break without

37
00:01:16,837 --> 00:01:18,637
experiencing any of it.

38
00:01:19,077 --> 00:01:21,267
You silenced the alarm and reached for

39
00:01:21,277 --> 00:01:22,277
the laptop again.

40
00:01:22,937 --> 00:01:23,957
Just finish this.

41
00:01:24,577 --> 00:01:26,687
Then you could finally stop thinking about

42
00:01:26,697 --> 00:01:27,217
work.

43
00:01:28,179 --> 00:01:29,399
Then your friend texted.

44
00:01:30,359 --> 00:01:32,789
They'd spent the afternoon lying around and

45
00:01:32,799 --> 00:01:34,299
felt terrible about it.

46
00:01:34,739 --> 00:01:37,559
Your reply came easily: you were exhausted.

47
00:01:38,459 --> 00:01:39,279
You needed a break.

48
00:01:39,919 --> 00:01:40,619
You hit send.

49
00:01:41,319 --> 00:01:42,779
A moment later, they asked:

50
00:01:43,279 --> 00:01:44,299
how's the movie?

51
00:01:44,679 --> 00:01:46,459
You looked at the untouched remote.

52
00:01:47,245 --> 00:01:49,685
You started typing: haven't earned it yet.

53
00:01:50,225 --> 00:01:50,665
Then stopped.

54
00:01:51,605 --> 00:01:53,085
You wouldn't actually send that.

55
00:01:53,385 --> 00:01:54,585
It sounded ridiculous.

56
00:01:55,505 --> 00:01:57,495
But looking at your evening, wasn't that

57
00:01:57,505 --> 00:01:59,045
the rule you were following?

58
00:01:59,525 --> 00:02:01,535
Your friend could rest because they were

59
00:02:01,545 --> 00:02:02,125
tired.

60
00:02:02,845 --> 00:02:04,885
You needed evidence that you'd done enough.

61
00:02:05,865 --> 00:02:07,815
Maybe that's part of what makes rest

62
00:02:07,825 --> 00:02:08,725
uncomfortable.

63
00:02:09,665 --> 00:02:11,695
If being useful has become a condition

64
00:02:11,705 --> 00:02:14,045
for feeling okay about yourself,

65
00:02:14,705 --> 00:02:17,465
an unfinished task can feel personal.

66
00:02:18,225 --> 00:02:20,445
The document can wait until morning.

67
00:02:21,045 --> 00:02:23,075
But can you feel okay about yourself

68
00:02:23,085 --> 00:02:24,145
while it waits?

69
00:02:24,951 --> 00:02:27,901
Research has linked seeing leisure as wasted

70
00:02:27,911 --> 00:02:30,091
time with enjoying it less.

71
00:02:30,931 --> 00:02:33,131
That doesn't explain everyone's guilt.

72
00:02:33,871 --> 00:02:36,561
In this story, though, every attempt to

73
00:02:36,571 --> 00:02:38,371
relax comes with an inspection:

74
00:02:39,171 --> 00:02:40,831
have I justified this yet?

75
00:02:41,971 --> 00:02:44,181
Imagine watching a movie while somebody keeps

76
00:02:44,191 --> 00:02:45,611
asking for your receipt.

77
00:02:46,385 --> 00:02:48,665
Sometimes the pressure comes from outside.

78
00:02:49,605 --> 00:02:51,555
A boss expects evening replies.

79
00:02:51,565 --> 00:02:54,305
Housework isn't shared fairly.

80
00:02:55,065 --> 00:02:56,565
Someone depends on you.

81
00:02:57,065 --> 00:02:59,875
Those situations may need practical help or

82
00:02:59,885 --> 00:03:00,465
boundaries.

83
00:03:01,465 --> 00:03:03,625
But tonight, the urgent work is done.

84
00:03:04,585 --> 00:03:06,255
Nobody has asked you to open that

85
00:03:06,265 --> 00:03:07,305
laptop again.

86
00:03:07,989 --> 00:03:09,249
You look at the document.

87
00:03:10,069 --> 00:03:11,289
One correction can wait.

88
00:03:12,029 --> 00:03:14,059
You write yourself a note: fix this

89
00:03:14,069 --> 00:03:15,529
tomorrow after breakfast.

90
00:03:16,389 --> 00:03:17,609
Then you close the laptop.

91
00:03:18,469 --> 00:03:20,019
You take the snack back to the

92
00:03:20,029 --> 00:03:20,509
couch.

93
00:03:21,289 --> 00:03:23,819
This time, you press play before finding

94
00:03:23,829 --> 00:03:25,269
another reason to leave.

95
00:03:26,073 --> 00:03:27,983
And right then, keys turn in the

96
00:03:27,993 --> 00:03:28,373
door.

97
00:03:29,033 --> 00:03:30,073
Your shoulders tighten.

98
00:03:30,953 --> 00:03:32,333
The familiar thought arrives:

99
00:03:33,033 --> 00:03:33,453
look busy.

100
00:03:34,253 --> 00:03:35,903
You hurry to the sink and grab

101
00:03:35,913 --> 00:03:37,833
a plate from the drying rack.

102
00:03:38,493 --> 00:03:40,593
Under the running water, you notice it.

103
00:03:41,013 --> 00:03:42,573
This plate was already clean.

104
00:03:43,754 --> 00:03:45,314
Your roommate walks in.

105
00:03:45,914 --> 00:03:47,194
Hey. How was your night?

106
00:03:47,834 --> 00:03:49,464
You almost say you were just cleaning

107
00:03:49,474 --> 00:03:52,414
up. Instead, you turn off the faucet.

108
00:03:52,834 --> 00:03:54,014
Set the plate down.

109
00:03:54,594 --> 00:03:56,754
Your mouth starts forming an explanation.

110
00:03:57,654 --> 00:03:58,794
You let that go too.

111
00:03:59,314 --> 00:04:00,734
I was watching a movie.

112
00:04:01,649 --> 00:04:03,369
Any good? You shake your head.

113
00:04:03,609 --> 00:04:04,309
You don't know yet.

114
00:04:04,569 --> 00:04:05,589
You've barely started.

115
00:04:06,009 --> 00:04:07,069
You sit back down.

116
00:04:07,809 --> 00:04:09,479
Your roommate takes a piece of your

117
00:04:09,489 --> 00:04:11,309
snack and heads down the hall.

118
00:04:11,889 --> 00:04:12,529
That's it.

119
00:04:13,209 --> 00:04:13,929
No inspection.

120
00:04:14,669 --> 00:04:16,239
You pick up the remote and find

121
00:04:16,249 --> 00:04:16,909
your place.

122
00:04:17,599 --> 00:04:19,899
The guilt hasn't magically disappeared.

123
00:04:20,859 --> 00:04:22,499
Neither has tomorrow's work.

124
00:04:23,199 --> 00:04:24,789
But this time, you stay for the

125
00:04:24,799 --> 00:04:25,499
next scene.

126
00:04:26,119 --> 00:04:26,879
Then the next.

127
00:04:27,479 --> 00:04:29,539
You let the movie hold your attention.

128
00:04:30,279 --> 00:04:32,019
And you let someone see you resting,

129
00:04:32,299 --> 00:04:33,709
without trying to make it look like

130
00:04:33,719 --> 00:04:34,499
something else.
